<title>EGYPT: Egypt cement firm ups 95/96 profits, yield.</title>
<headline>Egypt cement firm ups 95/96 profits, yield.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egypt's Helwan Portland Cement said on Thursday it raised net profits for financial year 1995/96 by 21 percent to 125.52 million pounds ($36.9 million) from 103.61 million a year earlier.</p>
<p>The financial year ended on June 30.</p>
<p>The partly-private firm, one of Egypt's leading cement manufacturers, also raised dividends for 1995/96 to five pounds from the 4.75 pounds it had promised investors earlier this year. Dividends for 1994/95 were four pounds per share.</p>
<p>The firm's net sales rose to 545 million pounds from 487 million in 1994/95.</p>
<p>The firm said it owned a 7.19 percent stake in partly private Suez Cement, one of Egypt's best performing cement companies.</p>
